---
LLMD serves model inference to clients. Running the server and connecting to an
existing server are separate starting points.

# [Start a server]($heading.id('start-a-server'))

Serve a model and send a chat, Decision, or embeddings request with the
[LLMD quickstart]($link.page('llmd/quickstart')). Choose a checkpoint, backend,
and decoding mode to generate launch and request commands for Docker or Homebrew.
See [Model and listener flags]($link.page('llmd/cli/model-and-listener')) for server startup,
[Docker options]($link.page('llmd/cli/docker-options')) for container settings,
and [Model compatibility]($link.page('llmd/models')) for routine test
configurations and published recipes.

After startup, check the loaded model with `/v1/models`. Use its ID in a chat
request. For a Decision checkpoint, send a state and a set of questions to
`/v1/systemone`. Follow [Ask structured questions with Decision]($link.page('llmd/decision'))
to read the selected labels and scores.

With `Qwen/Qwen3-Embedding-8B`, send text to `/v1/embeddings` to obtain a
vector for each input. Follow [Compare texts with embeddings]($link.page('llmd/text-similarity'))
to rank passages by their similarity to a query.

# [Connect an application]($heading.id('connect-an-application'))

Identify the server endpoint and exposed model name before sending a request.
The client and server must agree on the request format and model identifier.
Follow [Connect an application to LLMD]($link.page('llmd/developer-guide')) for a
Python client that discovers the model ID and sends a chat request. See
[Models]($link.page('llmd/api/models')) for model discovery and
[Chat completions]($link.page('llmd/api/chat-completions')) for streaming responses.

# [Operate the service]($heading.id('operate-the-service'))

Continue to [Operations]($link.page('operations')) to deploy, monitor, and
troubleshoot an LLMD service.
